<!--
    nexus-tk070.p5b (RDR-194 § D4, § P5b) — REWORKED 2026-08-20: DROP
    `nexus.migration_jobs`, not widen its PK.

    WHAT CHANGED AND WHY. This file originally shipped a composite-PK
    widening ((job_id) -> (tenant_id, job_id)) to close the one genuine
    tenant-keying gap D4 found. Stacked review (substantive-critic,
    T2 substantive-critique-tk070-p5b-2026-08-20) surfaced a CRITICAL
    finding the original D4 research missed: `nexus.migration_jobs` has ZERO
    live producers or consumers. `MigrationHandler.java` and
    `MigrationJobRepository.java` were DELETED at commit `7bcf29c67`
    (2026-07-24) — the RDR-178 Gap 5 async-ingest-cloud-job-tracking feature
    this table backed no longer exists in the service. Sam's disposition
    (2026-08-20, relayed via the orchestrator): DROP the table outright.
    Widening the PK of a table nothing writes to or reads from would have
    been correct-but-pointless; dropping dead schema is the actual fix. This
    SUPERSEDES the tenant-keying remedy D4 recorded for this table — see the
    CORRECTION blockquote at the RDR's own D4 section
    (`docs/rdr/rdr-194-fk-census-structural-schema-warts.md`, ~line 800) for
    the full disposition trail.

    DEATH EVIDENCE, restated here so this file is self-contained:
      - `MigrationHandler.java` + `MigrationJobRepository.java`: deleted at
        `7bcf29c67`.
      - Zero producers: nothing in `service/src/main/java` inserts, updates,
        or reads `nexus.migration_jobs` (grep confirms only a stale
        docstring/comment reference survives, in
        `CatalogRepository.java:6351` and this same file's own prior prose —
        no executable code path).
      - Zero consumers: no `/v1/migration/*` HTTP route registers a handler
        that touches this table any more.
      - The ONLY other Python reference is `src/nexus/health.py`'s RLS
        table-completeness list (removed in this same commit family — see
        that file's own comment for the chash_index/chash_alias precedent
        this follows) and the doctor's mirrored test list.
      - No wire claim is made about this table anywhere after this
        changeset: the caller-visible `job_id` handle D0.8 protected in the
        PK-widen version no longer has a live caller to protect, since the
        API surface that returned it is gone.

    IDX_MIGRATION_JOBS_ACTIVE_DEDUP goes with the table. `DROP TABLE`
    cascades both indexes (`idx_migration_jobs_tenant_created`,
    `idx_migration_jobs_active_dedup`) and the `tenant_isolation` RLS
    policy — nothing survives that needs a separate `DROP INDEX` /
    `DROP POLICY` statement (same cascade reasoning as
    `legacy-001-drop-chash-alias.xml`'s changeset 5, the precedent this
    changeset's shape follows).

    GRANTS SWEEP (checked, nothing to change). `grants-nexus-svc.xml` and
    `grants-nexus-diag.xml` grant via a `pg_class`-driven loop over
    `ALL TABLES` in the `nexus`/`t1` schemas (dynamic `EXECUTE 'GRANT ...
    ON %I.%I ...'`), never a per-table name list — dropping a table simply
    removes it from the next loop's iteration set, the same way
    `chash_alias`'s drop needed no grants-file edit. Neither grants file
    names `migration_jobs` literally (verified by grep across every
    changelog file); no runAlways grant references it, so no boot-time
    error risk from this drop.

    PRE-DROP ROW-COUNT NOTICE (the `fk-004-0-reconcile-precount` pattern,
    `fk-004-chunks-collection-registry.xml`, bead nexus-iq0qr): a drop of a
    POPULATED table must announce what it deleted, never silently. This
    changeset counts the row population before dropping, RAISE NOTICEs it,
    then drops — matching that precedent's shape (a read-only audit step
    ahead of the mutation, not a gate: the count is evidence, the drop
    proceeds regardless of its value, same "confirm-zero-or-delete-anyway"
    discipline `legacy-001-drop-chash-alias.xml`'s header states for its own
    deletes).

    SHAPE-AGNOSTIC / NEVER-WEDGE (migrations-never-wedge doctrine). The
    pre-count read and the `DROP TABLE` both tolerate the table already
    being absent: the count step checks `pg_class` for existence before
    touching the table (an unconditional `SELECT count(*) FROM
    nexus.migration_jobs` would error on a box where it is already gone),
    and the `DROP TABLE IF EXISTS` needs no matching guard at all. Neither
    statement assumes a particular prior schema state.

    RLS TOGGLE on the pre-count read ONLY. `migration_jobs` carries FORCE
    ROW LEVEL SECURITY (`migration-001-baseline.xml:102-103`). Liquibase
    runs as `nexus_admin`, NOT BYPASSRLS — an untoggled `SELECT count(*)`
    under FORCE RLS with no `nexus.tenant` GUC set would report 0 for every
    tenant regardless of actual content (the same silent-vacuity risk
    `catalog-029-1`/`legacy-001-1`/`legacy-001-2` toggle around). The `DROP
    TABLE` itself needs no toggle — DDL always sees the full physical table
    regardless of RLS, per this file's own prior header on the (now
    superseded) PK-widen version and `taxonomy-014`'s identical reasoning —
    and no FORCE restore is needed afterward since the table stops existing
    in the same changeset.

    D0.6 ROLLBACK: recreates `nexus.migration_jobs` EMPTY — the exact
    `migration-001-baseline.xml` shape (table, both indexes, RLS
    enable+force, `tenant_isolation` policy) — the only honest recreation.
    Whatever rows existed before this changeset ran are UNRECOVERABLE by
    construction, not an oversight (D0.6; `legacy-001-drop-chash-alias.xml`'s
    identical rollback discipline, itself citing the nexus-cck6z
    data-fidelity lesson: a rollback that cannot restore data must say so
    inline, never silently omit the gap).

    D0.1 placement UNCHANGED: this file stays at the changelog TAIL,
    immediately after `taxonomy-014-topics-tenant-unique.xml` and before the
    `grants-nexus-svc.xml` runAlways block — the rework only replaces this
    file's OWN content, not its position in `db.changelog-master.xml`.

    EXPECT_NEW_CHANGESETS=1 (unchanged from the PK-widen version — one
    changeset, same id `migration-002-1`, same author tag). Nothing else in
    the changelog tree changes shape as a result of this rework.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <!-- ── Changeset migration-002-1: DROP nexus.migration_jobs (dead table) ── -->
    <changeSet id="migration-002-1" author="nexus-tk070.p5b">
        <comment>
            RDR-194 D4 (reworked, Sam disposition 2026-08-20): nexus.migration_jobs
            is dead -- MigrationHandler.java + MigrationJobRepository.java deleted
            at 7bcf29c67 (2026-07-24), zero producers/consumers. DROP the table
            rather than widen its PK. Pre-drop row-count RAISE NOTICE (the
            fk-004-0-reconcile-precount pattern) so a populated table is never
            silently discarded. Shape-agnostic: tolerates the table already being
            absent. idx_migration_jobs_active_dedup and idx_migration_jobs_tenant_created
            go with the table via DROP TABLE's cascade -- no separate DROP INDEX.
            Rollback recreates the exact migration-001-baseline.xml shape, EMPTY
            (D0.6) -- any rows dropped here are unrecoverable.
        </comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
DO $$
DECLARE
    v_table_exists BOOLEAN;
    v_row_count BIGINT;
BEGIN
    SELECT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1 FROM pg_class c
        JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace
        WHERE n.nspname = 'nexus' AND c.relname = 'migration_jobs'
    ) INTO v_table_exists;

    IF v_table_exists THEN
        EXECUTE 'ALTER TABLE nexus.migration_jobs NO FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY';
        EXECUTE 'SELECT count(*) FROM nexus.migration_jobs' INTO v_row_count;
        RAISE NOTICE 'nexus-tk070.p5b: dropping nexus.migration_jobs (dead table -- MigrationHandler/MigrationJobRepository deleted 7bcf29c67, zero producers/consumers, RDR-194 D4 disposition 2026-08-20) -- % row(s) discarded, unrecoverable', v_row_count;
    ELSE
        RAISE NOTICE 'nexus-tk070.p5b: nexus.migration_jobs already absent -- nothing to drop';
    END IF;
END $$;

DROP TABLE IF EXISTS nexus.migration_jobs;
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <!-- Recreates nexus.migration_jobs EMPTY — the exact
                 migration-001-baseline.xml shape (table, both indexes, RLS
                 enable+force, tenant_isolation policy). Whatever rows existed
                 before this changeset ran are UNRECOVERABLE (D0.6) — this
                 rollback restores the SCHEMA the dead feature used to have,
                 not any data, matching legacy-001-drop-chash-alias.xml's
                 identical rollback discipline. -->
            <sql splitStatements="true" stripComments="false">
CREATE TABLE nexus.migration_jobs (
    job_id                TEXT         NOT NULL,
    tenant_id              TEXT         NOT NULL,
    state                   TEXT         NOT NULL DEFAULT 'queued',
    collections              JSONB        NOT NULL,
    collections_key          TEXT         NOT NULL,
    per_collection_counts    JSONB        NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}'::jsonb,
    started_at               TIMESTAMPTZ,
    finished_at              TIMESTAMPTZ,
    error                   TEXT,
    created_at               TIMESTAMPTZ  NOT NULL DEFAULT now(),
    CONSTRAINT migration_jobs_pk PRIMARY KEY (job_id),
    CONSTRAINT migration_jobs_state_chk CHECK (state IN ('queued', 'running', 'done', 'failed'))
);

CREATE INDEX idx_migration_jobs_tenant_created ON nexus.migration_jobs (tenant_id, created_at DESC);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX idx_migration_jobs_active_dedup
    ON nexus.migration_jobs (tenant_id, collections_key)
    WHERE state IN ('queued', 'running');

ALTER TABLE nexus.migration_jobs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
ALTER TABLE nexus.migration_jobs FORCE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

CREATE POLICY tenant_isolation ON nexus.migration_jobs
    USING      (tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true))
    WITH CHECK (tenant_id = current_setting('nexus.tenant', true));
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
